MERGE NOTE (knulli unified series): sm6115 'constrain BE format mask to S16_LE only' merged with sm8250 '0100-revert-force-16bit-audio' (only force S16_LE for compressed streams). The two cards share sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c, so the behaviour is keyed on card->driver_name: "sm4250" (qcom,qrb4210-rb2-sndcard, used by the sm6115 boards) gets the hard S16_LE constraint, everything else (qcom,sm8250-sndcard) gets the sm8250 behaviour.
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sm8250: per-card BE format fixup (S16_LE-only on sm4250, compressed-only on sm8250)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
index f193d0ba6..07c06b6ee 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6afe.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 #include <sound/soc.h>
 #include <sound/soc-dapm.h>
 #include <sound/pcm.h>
@@ -66,7 +67,17 @@ static int sm8250_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 
 	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;
 	channels->min = channels->max = 2;
-	snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
+
+	/*
+	 * sm4250/sm6115 cards (qrb4210-rb2-sndcard): constrain the BE format
+	 * mask to S16_LE only.
+	 * sm8250 cards: only force S16_LE for compressed playback and let the
+	 * format of every other stream be negotiated.
+	 */
+	if (rtd->card->driver_name && !strcmp(rtd->card->driver_name, "sm4250"))
+		params_set_format(params, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
+	else if (rtd->dai_link->compr_ops)
+		snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
 
 	return 0;
 }
